---
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import WordCounter from '../components/WordCounter.astro';
import { pagePath } from '../lib/site-path';
const base = Astro.site?.hostname === 'cthedj.github.io' ? '/mytoolmint/' : '/';
---
<ToolLayout title="Word Counter" metaTitle="Word Counter — Count Words, Characters & Reading Time | MyToolMint" description="Count words, characters, sentences, paragraphs and estimated reading time instantly. Paste or type text and keep it in your browser." category="Word tools" intro="Count words, characters, sentences and reading time as you write. Your text stays in your browser." path="/word-counter">
  <WordCounter slot="tool" />
  <section><h2>What the word counter measures</h2><p>The tool reports words, characters with and without spaces, sentences, paragraphs, estimated reading time and the most frequent meaningful words. Counts update as you type, so it works for quick drafts, notes and copy checks.</p></section>
  <section><h2>How words and characters are counted</h2><p>Sequences of letters or numbers are treated as words, including words with an internal apostrophe or hyphen. Character totals include every typed character, while the no-spaces total removes whitespace. Results can differ from a word processor because counting rules are not universal.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Reading-time estimate</h2><p>Reading time uses a simple pace of about 200 words per minute. Technical material, unfamiliar vocabulary and reading aloud can take longer, so treat the number as a practical estimate.</p></section>
  <section><h2>More word tools</h2><p>Need to solve a word puzzle instead of measure text? Try the <a href={pagePath('/five-letter-word-finder', base)}>Five-Letter Word Finder</a> to filter words by known positions and letters, the <a href={pagePath('/word-finder', base)}>Word Finder</a> for a letter rack and pattern, or the <a href={pagePath('/word-unscrambler', base)}>Word Unscrambler</a> to make words from a set of letters. Browse every related tool in <a href={pagePath('/word-tools', base)}>Word Tools</a>.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Privacy by design</h2><p>The counter runs locally in your browser. MyToolMint does not send the text to an application server or store it in a database. Avoid pasting sensitive text into any browser or device you do not trust.</p></section>
</ToolLayout>
